('127.249.d.4.A',4,'Charging a deposit before starting a large project helps by:','["Skipping contracts", "Reducing the risk of nonpayment", "Hiding costs", "Lowering prices"]'::jsonb,1,'Deposits protect cash flow.','original'),
('127.249.d.4.B',3,'Self-employed owners generally must keep records so they can:','["Lose receipts", "Avoid all taxes", "File accurate tax returns", "Hide income"]'::jsonb,2,'Records support taxes.','original'),
('127.249.d.4.B',4,'Receipts, invoices, and bank statements should be kept to:','["Lower income", "Avoid audits", "Fill drawers", "Document income and deductible expenses"]'::jsonb,3,'Documentation supports filings.','original'),
('127.249.d.4.C',3,'Recording each sale and expense in a ledger is:','["Bookkeeping", "Marketing", "Delivery", "Advertising"]'::jsonb,0,'Bookkeeping tracks transactions.','original'),
('127.249.d.4.C',4,'Keeping business and personal funds in separate accounts makes bookkeeping:','["More confusing", "Clearer and simpler", "Unnecessary", "Impossible"]'::jsonb,1,'Separation avoids confusion.','original'),
