('127.250.d.5.C',3,'Implementing a training program includes scheduling, trainers, and:','["Materials and facilities", "Delays", "Rumors", "Excuses"]'::jsonb,0,'Logistics support delivery.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.C',4,'Rolling out training in small sessions to avoid disrupting work is:','["Poor planning", "A practical implementation choice", "A layoff", "A violation"]'::jsonb,1,'Scheduling balances work.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.D',3,'Measuring whether trainees learned and used new skills is:','["Hiring", "Firing", "Evaluating the training program", "Recruiting"]'::jsonb,2,'Evaluation shows results.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.D',4,'A common way to evaluate training is to compare:','["Weather", "Logos", "Prices", "Performance before and after training"]'::jsonb,3,'Comparisons show improvement.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.E',3,'New employee orientation should cover company policies, safety rules, and:','["Job expectations and introductions", "Gossip", "Privileged data", "Rumors"]'::jsonb,0,'Orientation sets expectations.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.E',4,'Orientation helps new hires by:','["Hiding rules", "Reducing anxiety and speeding adjustment", "Cutting pay", "Raising turnover"]'::jsonb,1,'Good starts improve retention.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.F',3,'Learning job tasks while working under a skilled coworker''s guidance is:','["Orientation only", "A written test", "On-the-job training", "Classroom lecture only"]'::jsonb,2,'OJT is hands-on.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.F',4,'Besides on-the-job training, skills training can include:','["Rumors", "Waiting", "Gossip", "Apprenticeships and simulations"]'::jsonb,3,'Many formats exist.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.G',3,'New hires must be trained in proper Equal Employment Opportunity practices so they:','["Treat coworkers and customers fairly and lawfully", "Avoid training", "Hide complaints", "Ignore rules"]'::jsonb,0,'Training prevents violations.','original'),
('127.250.d.5.G',4,'Training on harassment prevention reduces the company''s:','["Training budget only", "Legal risk and workplace conflict", "Product line", "Customer base"]'::jsonb,1,'Prevention protects everyone.','original'),
('127.250.d.6.A',3,'Employees often need extra training to learn new technology and:','["Forget skills", "Avoid growth", "Update outdated skills", "Skip safety"]'::jsonb,2,'Skills change over time.','original'),
('127.250.d.6.A',4,'A company adopts new software. Employees will likely need:','["Layoffs only", "Pay cuts", "No support", "Additional training on the system"]'::jsonb,3,'New tools require training.','original'),
('127.250.d.6.B',3,'An appraisal program must comply with laws by being:','["Job-related and applied fairly", "Random", "Secret", "Biased"]'::jsonb,0,'Appraisals must be valid.','original'),
('127.250.d.6.B',4,'A fair appraisal form measures:','["Appearance only", "Performance on actual job duties", "Family status", "Age"]'::jsonb,1,'Criteria must relate to work.','original'),
('127.250.d.6.C',3,'Employees may be evaluated by supervisors and also by:','["Competitors", "No one", "Peers and customers", "Strangers only"]'::jsonb,2,'Multiple raters add perspective.','original'),
('127.250.d.6.C',4,'A 360-degree review collects feedback from:','["Only the boss", "Only the employee", "Only customers", "Supervisors, peers, and subordinates"]'::jsonb,3,'360 feedback is multi-source.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.A',3,'Compensation should reflect the job''s value and also meet the organization''s:','["Budget and goals", "Rumors", "Excuses", "Whims"]'::jsonb,0,'Pay must be affordable and aligned.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.A',4,'A company wants to attract skilled workers within a limited budget. Compensation must balance:','["Nothing", "Competitiveness and cost", "Secrecy", "Delay"]'::jsonb,1,'Pay is a tradeoff.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.B',3,'Factors that influence a pay system include the labor market, job worth, and:','["The employee''s hobbies", "Weather", "The organization''s ability to pay", "Sports scores"]'::jsonb,2,'Several factors set pay.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.B',4,'A shortage of skilled workers in a field usually pushes wages:','["Nowhere", "To zero", "Down", "Up"]'::jsonb,3,'Scarcity raises pay.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.C',3,'A salesperson who earns a percentage of each sale is paid by:','["Commission", "Piece rate", "Salary only", "Hourly wage"]'::jsonb,0,'Commission ties pay to sales.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.C',4,'A factory worker paid $2 per unit produced is paid by:','["Salary", "Piece rate", "Bonus only", "Commission"]'::jsonb,1,'Piece-rate pays per unit.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.D',3,'A wage and salary survey helps an employer:','["Close offices", "Set prices", "Compare its pay with what others pay", "Hide pay"]'::jsonb,2,'Surveys benchmark pay.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.D',4,'To perform a wage and salary survey, HR typically:','["Guesses", "Skips job titles", "Asks only competitors'' fans", "Collects pay data for similar jobs from comparable employers"]'::jsonb,3,'Benchmarking uses comparable data.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.E',3,'Pay that increases as an employee gains new skills is:','["Competence-based pay", "Overtime", "Piece rate", "Commission only"]'::jsonb,0,'Skills drive raises.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.E',4,'A benefit of competence-based pay is that it:','["Removes standards", "Encourages employees to learn more skills", "Lowers all pay", "Discourages growth"]'::jsonb,1,'Skills are rewarded.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.F',3,'The Fair Labor Standards Act sets federal rules on minimum wage and:','["Parking", "Dress code", "Overtime pay", "Vacation length"]'::jsonb,2,'FLSA covers minimum wage and overtime.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.F',4,'Under the FLSA, nonexempt employees working over 40 hours a week generally receive overtime of:','["No extra pay", "Double only", "Half their rate", "One and a half times their regular rate"]'::jsonb,3,'Overtime is time and a half.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.G',3,'A contemporary compensation issue is:','["Pay equity across genders and groups", "Candle prices", "Telegrams", "Typewriter ribbon"]'::jsonb,0,'Equity is a current concern.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.G',4,'Pay transparency laws require some employers to:','["Avoid posting jobs", "Disclose salary ranges for jobs", "Hide pay", "Cut pay"]'::jsonb,1,'Transparency reduces gaps.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.H',3,'A one-time payment for strong performance is a:','["Tax", "Salary", "Bonus", "Fine"]'::jsonb,2,'Bonuses reward results.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.H',4,'Sharing company profits with employees is called:','["Piece rate", "Overtime", "Commission only", "Profit sharing"]'::jsonb,3,'Profit sharing distributes earnings.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.I',3,'Executive pay becomes an ethical issue when it is:','["Much higher than company performance justifies", "Modest", "Fairly linked to results", "Disclosed"]'::jsonb,0,'Excess raises fairness concerns.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.I',4,'Large executive bonuses during layoffs may harm a company''s:','["Nothing", "Public relations and employee morale", "Product line", "Taxes only"]'::jsonb,1,'Optics affect trust.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.J',3,'To research executive compensation cases, a student can use:','["Rumors", "Gossip", "Company filings and credible news sites", "Guesses"]'::jsonb,2,'Public filings are reliable.','original'),
('127.250.d.7.J',4,'A public company reports executive pay in its:','["Lunch menu", "Parking permit", "Newsletter only", "Proxy statement filed with the SEC"]'::jsonb,3,'Proxy statements disclose pay.','original'),
('127.250.d.8.A',3,'Federal law requires employers to pay Social Security and Medicare taxes under the:','["Federal Insurance Contributions Act", "Sherman Act", "Clean Water Act", "Tariff Act"]'::jsonb,0,'FICA funds these programs.','original'),
('127.250.d.8.A',4,'Employers must also pay into state and federal:','["Parking funds", "Unemployment insurance", "Gym memberships", "Vacation funds"]'::jsonb,1,'Unemployment insurance is mandatory.','original'),
('127.250.d.8.B',3,'Health insurance, paid time off, and retirement plans are:','["Fines", "Taxes", "Discretionary benefits", "Mandated benefits"]'::jsonb,2,'Employers choose to offer them.','original'),
('127.250.d.8.B',4,'A 401(k) plan is a common:','["Health claim", "Vacation policy", "Tax form", "Retirement benefit"]'::jsonb,3,'401(k)s help employees save.','original'),
('127.250.d.8.C',3,'Employee assistance programs and tuition reimbursement are:','["Ancillary services", "Penalties", "Fines", "Taxes"]'::jsonb,0,'They are extra services.','original'),
('127.250.d.8.C',4,'Offering on-site child care or wellness programs is an example of:','["Mandated benefits", "Ancillary services", "Wages", "Overtime"]'::jsonb,1,'Extras support employees.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.A',3,'The Occupational Safety and Health Act requires employers to provide:','["Free lunch", "Unlimited pay", "A workplace free from recognized hazards", "Short shifts"]'::jsonb,2,'OSHA sets safety duties.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.A',4,'The agency that enforces workplace safety laws is:','["The SEC", "The EEOC", "The FDA", "OSHA"]'::jsonb,3,'OSHA enforces safety standards.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.B',3,'Right-to-know laws give employees information about:','["Hazardous chemicals they work with", "Hiring plans", "Coworkers'' pay", "Company profits"]'::jsonb,0,'Hazard communication protects workers.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.B',4,'Safety Data Sheets are used to inform workers about:','["Pay rates", "The hazards of chemicals and how to handle them", "Vacation plans", "Parking"]'::jsonb,1,'SDSs communicate hazards.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.C',3,'A safety awareness program might include posters, training, and:','["No communication", "Secret rules", "Regular safety drills and meetings", "Penalties only"]'::jsonb,2,'Programs build safe habits.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.C',4,'To promote safety awareness, a manager can:','["Punish reporting", "Ignore reports", "Hide accidents", "Recognize safe behavior and share near-miss lessons"]'::jsonb,3,'Open reporting improves safety.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.D',3,'Enforcing workplace safety rules is necessary to:','["Prevent injuries and avoid fines", "Annoy staff", "Slow work", "Raise costs only"]'::jsonb,0,'Enforcement protects people.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.D',4,'A worker repeatedly ignores required protective gear. The manager should:','["Ignore it", "Apply consistent corrective action", "Reward it", "Hide the issue"]'::jsonb,1,'Consistent enforcement keeps rules credible.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.E',3,'After a workplace accident, the employer must:','["Hide it", "Ignore it", "Record and investigate the incident", "Delay indefinitely"]'::jsonb,2,'Investigation prevents recurrence.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_43_v1'
from (values
('127.250.d.9.E',4,'The goal of an accident investigation is to find:','["An excuse", "Someone to blame", "A reason to delay", "The root cause so it can be prevented"]'::jsonb,3,'Root cause analysis prevents repeats.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.F',3,'A way to prevent workplace violence is:','["Clear policies, training, and a reporting process", "Ignoring threats", "Removing security", "Hiding incidents"]'::jsonb,0,'Prevention requires policy and training.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.F',4,'An employee reports a threat from a coworker. HR should:','["Ignore it", "Take it seriously and investigate promptly", "Wait a year", "Dismiss it"]'::jsonb,1,'Threats need prompt action.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.G',3,'Employers can help employees manage workplace stress by offering:','["No breaks", "More pressure", "Counseling resources and reasonable workloads", "Longer shifts"]'::jsonb,2,'Support reduces stress.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.G',4,'Chronic workplace stress can lead to:','["Lower turnover", "Less conflict", "Better health", "Lower productivity and higher absenteeism"]'::jsonb,3,'Stress harms performance.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.H',3,'To research a workplace violence case, a student should use:','["Credible news and legal sources", "Gossip", "Rumors", "Guesses"]'::jsonb,0,'Reliable sources matter.','original'),
('127.250.d.9.H',4,'When analyzing a violence case, a student should look for:','["Only gossip", "What warning signs were missed and how to prevent recurrence", "Only blame", "Nothing"]'::jsonb,1,'Analysis focuses on prevention.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.A',3,'Employee rights, such as fair pay and safe conditions, are balanced by employer:','["Fears", "Hobbies", "Responsibilities and legitimate business needs", "Jokes"]'::jsonb,2,'Rights and duties coexist.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.B',3,'Progressive discipline usually starts with:','["A promotion", "A raise", "Termination", "A verbal warning"]'::jsonb,3,'Discipline escalates in steps.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.B',4,'Documenting each disciplinary step is important because it:','["Provides a record if the decision is challenged", "Lowers morale", "Hides actions", "Replaces training"]'::jsonb,0,'Documentation protects fairness.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.C',3,'Before discharging an employee, HR should:','["Act on impulse", "Review documentation and follow policy and law", "Skip records", "Ignore rules"]'::jsonb,1,'Proper process avoids claims.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.C',4,'An exit interview helps the organization:','["Hide issues", "Keep secrets", "Learn why employees leave", "Avoid feedback"]'::jsonb,2,'Exit data reveals problems.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.D',3,'Using mediation or arbitration instead of court to settle a workplace dispute is:','["Strike", "Litigation", "Lockout", "Alternative Dispute Resolution"]'::jsonb,3,'ADR avoids court.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.D',4,'A benefit of Alternative Dispute Resolution is that it is usually:','["Faster and less costly than court", "More public", "Slower", "Always binding on no one"]'::jsonb,0,'ADR saves time and money.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.E',3,'The federal law that protects workers'' right to organize and bargain collectively is the:','["Sherman Act", "National Labor Relations Act", "Clean Air Act", "Tariff Act"]'::jsonb,1,'The Wagner Act (NLRA) protects organizing.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.E',4,'The Taft-Hartley Act is best known for:','["Setting minimum wage", "Creating Social Security", "Restricting certain union and strike practices", "Banning all unions"]'::jsonb,2,'It amended the Wagner Act.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.F',3,'Employees may join a union to seek better pay, benefits, and:','["Fewer rights", "Less pay", "More hazards", "Working conditions"]'::jsonb,3,'Unions bargain for improvements.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.F',4,'Workers often unionize because they want:','["A collective voice with management", "Isolation", "Lower pay", "Less safety"]'::jsonb,0,'Collective bargaining gives workers leverage.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.G',3,'During a union organizing drive, an employer may NOT:','["Share facts", "Threaten or fire workers for supporting the union", "Post legal notices", "Answer questions"]'::jsonb,1,'Retaliation is an unfair labor practice.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.G',4,'During unionization, an employer may lawfully:','["Threaten layoffs", "Promise rewards for voting no", "Share factual information about the company''s position", "Spy on meetings"]'::jsonb,2,'Truthful communication is allowed.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.H',3,'A union''s local chapter is run by:','["The employer", "The government", "Random strangers", "Elected officers and stewards"]'::jsonb,3,'Locals are member-led.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.H',4,'A union steward typically:','["Represents members in grievances", "Owns the company", "Hires managers", "Sets stock prices"]'::jsonb,0,'Stewards support members.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.I',3,'The AFL-CIO is a:','["Federal agency", "Federation of national and international unions", "Corporation", "Court"]'::jsonb,1,'It unites many unions.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.I',4,'A national union is made up of many:','["Banks", "Courts", "Local unions", "Companies"]'::jsonb,2,'Locals affiliate with nationals.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.J',3,'Negotiations between a union and an employer over wages, hours, and conditions are:','["A lockout", "A boycott", "Arbitration only", "Collective bargaining"]'::jsonb,3,'Bargaining produces the contract.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.J',4,'The written agreement resulting from bargaining is the:','["Collective bargaining agreement", "Business plan", "Resume", "Invoice"]'::jsonb,0,'The CBA sets terms.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.K',3,'A formal process for resolving a worker''s complaint under a union contract is a:','["Pay cut", "Grievance procedure", "Marketing plan", "Hiring plan"]'::jsonb,1,'Grievances follow steps.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.K',4,'A typical grievance begins with:','["A lawsuit", "A strike", "The employee and steward talking to the supervisor", "A lockout"]'::jsonb,2,'First step is informal discussion.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.L',3,'When a grievance cannot be settled, a neutral third party may decide in:','["A strike", "Mediation only", "A boycott", "Grievance arbitration"]'::jsonb,3,'The arbitrator''s decision is typically final.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.L',4,'The decision of a grievance arbitrator is usually:','["Final and binding", "Ignored", "Advisory only", "Optional"]'::jsonb,0,'Arbitration resolves disputes.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.M',3,'A challenge facing unions today is:','["Free labor", "Declining membership in many industries", "No challenges", "Rising membership everywhere"]'::jsonb,1,'Union density has fallen.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.M',4,'Global competition and automation present unions with:','["Higher membership only", "No change", "Pressure on jobs and bargaining power", "Easy bargaining"]'::jsonb,2,'Economic change challenges unions.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.N',3,'To research labor relations cases online, a student should use:','["Guesses", "Gossip", "Rumors", "Court, agency, and news reports from reliable sources"]'::jsonb,3,'Credible sources matter.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.N',4,'The federal agency that handles unfair labor practice charges is the:','["National Labor Relations Board", "EEOC", "FDA", "SEC"]'::jsonb,0,'The NLRB enforces labor law.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.A',3,'An international HR issue is how to:','["Print letters", "Staff and manage employees in different countries", "Buy chairs", "Paint offices"]'::jsonb,1,'Global HR spans borders.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.A',4,'HR in a multinational must understand that employment laws:','["Are optional", "Are identical", "Differ from country to country", "Do not exist"]'::jsonb,2,'Local laws vary.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.B',3,'Recruiting for an overseas post may involve choosing between expatriates and:','["Strangers", "Robots", "Competitors", "Local hires"]'::jsonb,3,'Firms weigh sending staff versus hiring locally.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.B',4,'An issue in selecting expatriates is whether the candidate and family can:','["Adapt to a new culture", "Avoid people", "Ignore language", "Skip training"]'::jsonb,0,'Adaptability predicts success.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.C',3,'Paying an expatriate more because of high living costs abroad is a:','["Fine", "Cost-of-living adjustment", "Tax cut", "Penalty"]'::jsonb,1,'Adjustments maintain standard of living.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.C',4,'Expatriate pay packages often add allowances for housing and:','["Hobbies", "Gifts", "Education for children", "Pets"]'::jsonb,2,'Allowances ease relocation.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.D',3,'A common problem for employees returning from abroad is:','["No change", "No pay", "Too little experience", "Reentry adjustment and career placement"]'::jsonb,3,'Repatriation is difficult.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.D',4,'A solution to repatriation problems is:','["Planning the employee''s next role before they return", "Ignoring them", "Hiding openings", "Cutting pay"]'::jsonb,0,'Planning eases return.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.E',3,'In many countries, unions are stronger than in the U.S. and may have a role in:','["Only sports", "Setting company policies and working conditions", "Nothing", "Only tourism"]'::jsonb,1,'Labor environments differ.','original'),
('127.250.d.11.E',4,'Works councils in some European nations give employees:','["Ownership", "Exemption from laws", "A voice in workplace decisions", "No say"]'::jsonb,2,'Councils represent workers.','original'),
('127.250.d.12.A',3,'Respecting coworkers'' views and sharing the workload is:','["Indifference", "Poor teamwork", "Rudeness", "Effective teamwork"]'::jsonb,3,'Teamwork builds results.','original'),
('127.250.d.12.A',4,'A team member who listens actively and resolves conflicts shows:','["Strong interpersonal skills", "No skills", "Negative traits", "Weak skills"]'::jsonb,0,'Communication skills matter.','original'),
('127.250.d.12.B',3,'Running for an office in a student HR club is a:','["Hiring practice", "Leadership activity", "Audit", "Tariff"]'::jsonb,1,'Offices develop leadership.','original'),
('127.250.d.12.B',4,'Interviewing an HR professional about their career is a:','["Layoff", "Disciplinary action", "Career development activity", "Tax filing"]'::jsonb,2,'Informational interviews explore careers.','original'),
('127.250.d.10.A',5,'A nonunion employee is fired after reporting unsafe machinery to a state inspector. Which concept does this most directly raise?','["A wage and salary survey", "An employer responsibility to hide hazards", "A union grievance deadline", "An employee right to protection that limits employer discretion"]'::jsonb,3,'Employees may report hazards without retaliation.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
